#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:209
msgid "Automatically, when a file changes — recommended"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:211
msgid "Browser caching keeps working at full strength; files are re-downloaded only after they really change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:215
msgid "On every page load (development mode; styles & scripts only)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:221
msgid "Every"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:223
msgid "minutes (legacy)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:229
msgid "Only manually — with the \"Update versions\" button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:235
msgid "Show the \"Update versions\" button on the toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: page cache plugin name.
#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:246
#, php-format
msgid "Also clear the %s page cache when versions are updated"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:251
msgid "The page cache stores HTML that still references old file versions. Clearing it together with the version update means every visitor sees the new site immediately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:260
msgid "Refresh versions automatically after plugin, theme or WordPress updates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:262
msgid "Updates change CSS and JS files. With this on, visitors get the new files right after every update (including automatic ones) — no need to press \"Update versions\". Works together with the page cache option above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:268
msgid "update"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: human-readable time difference, e.g. "2 hours", 2: update type, e.g. "plugin update".
#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:272
#, php-format
msgid "Last automatic refresh: %1$s ago (%2$s)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:282
msgid "The toolbar button is disabled, so nothing will ever update the versions. Enable the toolbar button above, or use the \"Update versions now\" button on this page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:287
msgid "Speed up:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:291
msgid "Let browsers keep static files for a year"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:293
msgid "Serves CSS, JS, fonts and images with long-lived caching headers, so repeat visits load faster. Safe: a file's URL changes whenever the file changes, so visitors still see updates immediately. Also fixes the Lighthouse audit \"Serve static assets with an efficient cache policy\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:296
msgid "Requires the \"Styles & scripts\" option above — long caching is only safe while file URLs are versioned."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: human-readable time difference, e.g. "2 hours".
#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:305
#, php-format
msgid "✓ Long browser caching is active — verified on this site %s ago. Saving the settings re-checks it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:312
msgid "Warning: the caching headers are not showing up yet. Possible reasons: the server ignores .htaccess, lacks the mod_headers / mod_expires modules, or WordPress cannot write to the .htaccess file. Ask your host, or add the rules below to the server configuration manually. Saving the settings re-checks this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:316
msgid "Could not verify the headers automatically (the site could not reach itself). Check a CSS file's Cache-Control response header in your browser's developer tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:323
msgid "Server rules for long browser caching"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:325
msgid "On multisite the plugin never edits the shared .htaccess automatically — add the rules to the server configuration manually."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:330
msgid "Add this to your nginx server block (inside server { … }) and reload nginx:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-prevent-browser-caching-admin-settings.php:332
msgid "Add this to the .htaccess file in your WordPress root folder (or ask your host to):"
msgstr ""

